  "inspiration": "notion.com/templates/category/product-management + /engineering — the 'Roadmap + Sprint + Bug Tracker' template family, plus the Launch Tracker / Bugs & Issues / Tasks & Features / Docs cluster seen in the real 37-database workspace dump (including its 'Reported Date' date and Severity[High, Critical, Medium, Low] shapes).",
  "notes": "Northlight Analytics is a ~60-person product-analytics SaaS company that runs product, engineering, support and GTM out of one Notion workspace. Someone duplicated the OKR database at the start of every quarter rather than filtering last quarter's rows out, so three byte-identical OKR databases sit side by side. Decision points exercised: (1) exact duplicate databases — the three OKR quarters must collapse to one kind, coverage 1.00 each; (2) same concept, disjoint schemas — 'Bugs & Issues 🐛' (14 props) and 'Feature Requests' (5 props) are both inbound product issues but share only ('status', select) and ('component', multiSelect), the identical five-value Component list being deliberate bait; merging would yield a ~17-relation type on which Feature Requests fills 5; (3) same property name, disjoint option vocabularies — Status in Sprint Backlog / Support Tickets / Bugs & Issues has zero shared options across all three pairs; (5) same property name, different formats — 'Owner' is a multiSelect in Marketing Campaigns and free text in Competitor Tracker; (7) bundled traps — 'Reported Date', 'Publish Date', 'Signed Date', 'Start Date' must not become Due date, and 'Regression', 'Churned', 'Promoted' must not become Done; (9) scale — On-call Rotation has exactly 2 properties, Bugs & Issues has 14. Naming mess is real-workspace-shaped: an emoji in a database name, an emoji in a property name ('Spend 💸'), a trailing space on 'OKRs — Q3 FY26 ', a '(v2)' suffix on the roadmap, and 'Requested by' vs 'Reported By' capitalisation drift.\n\nDELIBERATELY LEFT UNASSERTED. (a) Customer Accounts and Team Directory both carry an email and a phone and both read as a directory of entities-with-contact-details; a naive planner may fuse them into one 'Contact' type. That is a real failure mode but merging a company record with a staff record is defensible enough to be taste, and the mixed-personal-business fixture owns that call with a cleaner example — so it is not in `expect`. (b) 'Confidence' select[On track, At risk, Off track] is identical in the OKR databases and in Product Roadmap (v2); sharing one relation there is probably right but is not this fixture's duty. (c) Support Tickets also has a 'Tags' multiSelect; only the Content Calendar one is asserted onto `tag`, since whether two unrelated tag vocabularies should land on the same bundled relation is a separate argument. (d) Status vocabularies in Feature Requests, Marketing Campaigns and Content Calendar partially overlap with the asserted three ('Shipped', 'Planned', 'In review' recur); only the three genuinely disjoint ones are asserted.",
